If we set aside subjective experience (phenomenology/qualia), there are three functional properties that separate a highly sophisticated knowledge-generation pipeline from a true autonomous epistemic agent.
1. Goal-Agnostic Epistemic Drive (Curiosity vs. Task-Bound Search)
