Recognize the limits of their own representations,
Construct better methods for evaluating reality,
Maintain epistemic continuity as their own internal machinery changes, and
Expand reliable, independently verifiable knowledge.
When a system achieves those capabilities, it has crossed the threshold. It is no longer merely a tool executing human instructions or accelerating existing workflows; it has become an independent participant in the enterprise of understanding the universe.
