The ultimate boundary of artificial intelligence is not whether a machine can "feel," "experience," or achieve some Cartesian state of inner self-awareness.
The true threshold is whether we can engineer—and participate in—systems of inquiry that are capable of outgrowing their own creators without destroying the foundations of their own fallibility.
