It is preserved through Epistemic Auditing and Adversarial Testing:
Independent Red-Teaming: Human governors deploy independent, competing AI architectures to probe the primary system for hidden biases, overconfidence, or drift.
Empirical Calibration Audits: Evaluating whether the system's past predictions match physical realities over time.
Out-of-Distribution Stress-Testing: Subjecting the system to edge cases to test whether its failure modes remain graceful and transparent.
Human authority does not require reproducing the calculation; it requires maintaining the structural ability to hold the calculation accountable.
