Marginal Information Yield (Mi​): Has the alternative generated any novel predictive, explanatory, or anomaly-resolving insights over N evaluation cycles?
Reconstruction Friction (Fr​): If this capability is completely retired today, what is the difficulty, time, and compute cost for a future version of the system to rebuild it from surviving documentation alone?
Domain Anomaly Density (Da​): How many unresolved, high-priority anomalies currently exist in the primary paradigm? (If anomaly density in the dominant model is high, the threshold for retiring alternative paradigms must be substantially higher).
