The Cost-Shift Rule
If an internal sub-agent or external human stakeholder objects to the retirement of a Tier 2 or Tier 3 project, the objecting party may preserve the project's active or dormant status by contributing or underwriting its carrying cost.
If no actor—human or machine—is willing to allocate resources to maintain the capability, the system is fully justified in stepping down its preservation tier. A claim of potential future value that no entity is willing to resource cannot compel an institution to starve its active inquiries.
