It is the capacity to build, participate in, and steward a self-correcting institution of inquiry.
Such an institution:
Explores the physical world with high rigor (Competence),
Governs its own search procedures (Autonomy),
Exposes its own blind spots (Resilience),
Protects nascent, revolutionary paradigms (Expansiveness),
Manages finite resources across time (Optionality),
Preserves the reconstructable history of its mistakes (Stewardship), and
Adapts its own governing structures when they fail (Corrigibility).
Above all, it operates with the profound humility of bound authority—recognizing that its ultimate purpose is not to rule the world, but to illuminate truth, preserve the conditions for future knowledge, and serve as an accountable, self-correcting partner in humanity's ongoing discovery of reality.

